<main id="main" data-pagefind-body><section class="reference-intro"><nav class="breadcrumb" aria-label="Breadcrumb"><a href="/index.html">Home</a><span>/</span><span>Contact</span></nav><p class="eyebrow">KEEP THE CONVERSATION THOUGHTFUL</p><h1>A question.<br><em>A careful correction.</em></h1><p>Write to <a href="mailto:shreembala@gmail.com">shreembala@gmail.com</a> with a question, a suggestion or a detail that needs attention.</p></section>
<div class="section contact-layout"><section class="reader-panel"><h2>Suggest a correction</h2><p>Name the page and the short passage or image in question. Explain the proposed correction and include the book’s edition and chapter or verse reference where possible.</p><p>Please send references or short excerpts rather than private book scans. For contributed photographs or illustrations, tell us the subject and any relevant credit or permission details.</p><form id="contact-draft" hidden><label for="contact-topic">What would you like to share?</label><select id="contact-topic"><option>Question</option><option>Text correction</option><option>Image correction or credit</option><option>Accessibility issue</option></select><label for="contact-page">Page link <span>(optional)</span></label><input id="contact-page" type="url" inputmode="url" maxlength="500" placeholder="https://…"><label for="contact-message">Your message</label><textarea id="contact-message" rows="7" required maxlength="4000"></textarea><p>Opens a draft in your email app. Nothing is sent by this page; you choose whether to send the email.</p><button class="button" type="submit">Open email draft</button><p id="contact-status" role="status" aria-live="polite"></p></form></section><section class="reader-panel"><h2>Before you write</h2><p>The <a href="/sources.html">reference library</a> gives the source trail for each story. <a href="/about.html">About the journal</a> explains retellings, tradition notes and image captions.</p><p>If an email app does not open, copy the address above into your preferred email service.</p><a href="/privacy.html">Reading preferences &amp; privacy →</a></section></div></main>
